(7428144, 1173114, 163081, '<td valign="top">My favorite for a ribbon. I give it a 9 and my Yellow Dragon Award<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1173263" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/160000-164999/163081/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1173263.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/160000-164999/163081/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1173263.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/160000-164999/163081/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1173263.jpg"/></a></td>', 'My favorite for a ribbon. I give it a 9 and my Yellow Dragon Award', '2016-01-14 11:01:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(7428162, 1173208, 38032, '<td valign="top">This did not leave an impression on me when I first saw it. Looking back, bumping up. The textures, streaks and movement create a strong blend of tones and mystery. There does seem to be a man there, however, which makes it just earthly enough to wonder for a while. Also: seeing what appears to be sensor dust makes me wonder if the movement was, in fact, all outside of the lens.</td>', 'This did not leave an impression on me when I first saw it. Looking back, bumping up. The textures, streaks and movement create a strong blend of tones and mystery. There does seem to be a man there, however, which makes it just earthly enough to wonder for a while. Also: seeing what appears to be sensor dust makes me wonder if the movement was, in fact, all outside of the lens.', '2016-01-14 11:52:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(7428172, 1173468, 100393, '<td valign="top">This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more. <br/> <br/>This is one of my 10s - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: <br/> <br/>1. I''m a fan of blur - this is an easy pick for me<br/>2. Great POV, we don''t see much from these sorts of perspectives<br/>3. The faded tones, again - I''m a fan<br/>4. The beast itself, headless and ambiguous - great stuff<br/> <br/>Overall, a lovely image that shuns a conventional aesthetic for something far more engaging.</td>', 'This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier)  Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more.  This is one of my 10s - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:  1. I''m a fan of blur - this is an easy pick for me2. Great POV, we don''t see much from these sorts of perspectives3. The faded tones, again - I''m a fan4. The beast itself, headless and ambiguous - great stuff Overall, a lovely image that shuns a conventional aesthetic for something far more engaging.', '2016-01-14 13:58:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(7428173, 1173332, 100393, '<td valign="top">This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more. <br/> <br/>This is one of my 10s - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: <br/> <br/>1. Superbly bold and simultaneously subtle<br/>2. I love the overlap of the figures/reflections<br/>3. The subtle nudity, mannequin?<br/>4. The coloration and the grain<br/> <br/>Overall this an amazingly engaging image - one that shuns convention for something altogether more interesting.<br/> <br/>Awarded for the 2015 Art of 2015:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1051747" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100393/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1051747.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100393/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1051747.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100393/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1051747.jpg"/></a></td>', 'This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier)  Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more.  This is one of my 10s - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:  1. Superbly bold and simultaneously subtle2. I love the overlap of the figures/reflections3. The subtle nudity, mannequin?4. The coloration and the grain Overall this an amazingly engaging image - one that shuns convention for something altogether more interesting. Awarded for the 2015 Art of 2015: ', '2016-01-14 14:11:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(7428175, 1173250, 100393, '<td valign="top">This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more. <br/> <br/>This is one of my 10s - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: <br/> <br/>1. What an ambience you have captured!<br/>2. Wonderful tones<br/>3. Engaging subjects<br/>4. Amazing light<br/>5. Great and confident use of space and how to use it to excellent effect<br/>6. The great vignette, I like how it steers the eye.<br/> <br/>Overall, I wouldn''t be surprised if this takes the Blue. I suspect it will engage those with conventional photographic tastes as well as those who reward the more eclectic.</td>', 'This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier)  Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more.  This is one of my 10s - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:  1. What an ambience you have captured!2. Wonderful tones3. Engaging subjects4. Amazing light5. Great and confident use of space and how to use it to excellent effect6. The great vignette, I like how it steers the eye. Overall, I wouldn''t be surprised if this takes the Blue. I suspect it will engage those with conventional photographic tastes as well as those who reward the more eclectic.', '2016-01-14 14:29:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(7428177, 1173453, 100393, '<td valign="top">This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more. <br/> <br/>This is one of my 10s - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: <br/> <br/>1. Superb composition<br/>2. Wonderful coloration<br/>3. Dynamism and stillness - in magical simultaneity.<br/> <br/>Overall, an image that is really successful in offering more than the sum of its parts.</td>', 'This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier)  Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more.  This is one of my 10s - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:  1. Superb composition2. Wonderful coloration3. Dynamism and stillness - in magical simultaneity. Overall, an image that is really successful in offering more than the sum of its parts.', '2016-01-14 14:33:04.000000', NULL, 1),
