(7429767, 1173453, 68504, '<td valign="top">I meant to get back to this one in the voting/commenting. As tate said, David Hockney sprang to mind, but this is so not a painting by DH. All that colourful noisy snow sprinkling down, and then the sheer magic of the white light and the golden arches. We feel the happening, but the construction is so strong we wonder if it isn''t wholly a trick, a trick of the mind like the way we remember embracing the snow as children.</td>', 'I meant to get back to this one in the voting/commenting. As tate said, David Hockney sprang to mind, but this is so not a painting by DH. All that colourful noisy snow sprinkling down, and then the sheer magic of the white light and the golden arches. We feel the happening, but the construction is so strong we wonder if it isn''t wholly a trick, a trick of the mind like the way we remember embracing the snow as children.', '2016-01-18 16:06:02.000000', NULL, 0),
